sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Access and Onboarding (F-02); docs/adr/ADR-003-country-isolation.md
desc:
"Where do you practise?" with India (Azure Central India · DPDP Act · ABDM integration available) and UAE (Azure UAE North · separate deployment · DoH/DHA/MOHAP per emirate) cards. Explains data stays in-country and cannot be moved later without a new account and export. "Continue in {region}" routes sign-up to that country's deployment; if a country is not yet live, it captures interest instead.
ac:
- Selecting a region and continuing creates the tenant only in that country's deployment; tenant.country_code and residency_region are immutable afterwards (domain test).
- The residency explanation text matches the design and is translated.
- If the selected country deployment is not live, the user sees a waitlist form (no PHI) instead of sign-up.
- The selection is recorded in the onboarding audit trail.

=== MDV-P1-003
status: Done
progress:
- [PR #57](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/57) (re-opened from #54, which merged into a stale branch): /trust with the six designed blocks and footer; policy versions and sub-processors from PublicSite/trust-centre.json (reloads on change, overridable by app settings, versioned in git), each with its effective date or "Not yet in effect"
- Demo request form (contact fields only, patient-information warning): server validation, anti-forgery, 5/hour per client, honeypot and minimum fill time; stored by the new Leads module (leads schema, insert/read-only role) and emailed to the founder without the free-text message (local SMTP sink)
