sources: PRD v2 P1-04; docs/02-design/source/Medvya Clinician App (Schedule, settings hours); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#schedule-p-04--medvya-clinician-app
desc:
Per doctor and location: weekly template (weekday, start, end, room/resource), breaks (e.g. lunch), default slot length (15/20/30 min) and per-visit-type length (e.g. new consult 40 min = 2 slots). Facility time zone; all times stored UTC and displayed in facility time. Resources (procedure room) can be scheduled like a doctor column. Generates bookable slots on the fly (no pre-materialised slot table required) or materialises slots per day — decision recorded.
ac:
- Given a template Mon–Fri 09:00–13:00 and 17:00–20:00 with 20-minute slots, then the calendar shows bookable slots exactly in those windows in facility local time.
- Breaks and closed days show as Unavailable (hatched) with the reason and cannot be booked.
- Changing a template affects only future unbooked slots; existing appointments outside new hours are listed for action.
- Visit types can span multiple slots and the calendar renders them spanning.
- Daylight-saving-free zones (IST, GST) and a test zone with DST are handled correctly (unit tests).

