confidence: 88 | Designed interaction (click empty slot → book); hold mechanism specified in P1-07.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Clinician App (Schedule); PRD v2 P1-06, P1-07
desc:
Clicking an empty slot opens the booking panel for that doctor/resource and time; select or register a patient, visit type (sets length), reason category (free-text reason never shown on reception screens beyond category), channel. A slot hold (default 2 minutes) reserves the slot while the receptionist completes the form; confirmation creates the appointment and triggers the confirmation message (MDV-P1-032).
ac:
- Opening the booking panel creates a hold; another user trying the same slot sees it as "being booked" and cannot confirm it.
- Holds expire automatically after the configured time and the slot becomes free.
- A booking for an unavailable column (doctor not working) is impossible from UI and API.
- Booking writes AppointmentBooked.v1 (no PHI) and an audit event; the appointment appears on the board in Booked.
- Booking API p95 < 300 ms under the P1 load profile (MDV-P1-037).

=== MDV-P1-022
status: Partly done
progress:
- Merged [PR #60](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/60): SCHEDULE_SLOT rows per 5-minute unit with a unique index on (calendar, location, slot start); every hold and booking in a SERIALIZABLE transaction after `sp_getapplock` per doctor-day; deadlocks and lock timeouts retried, then "busy"; 100 parallel bookings or holds of one slot give exactly one on Testcontainers SQL Server (also overlapping multi-slot); mutation-checked (unique index, lock, all guards: 16 double bookings without them)
- Merged [PR #80](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/80): cancel, no-show and reschedule free the visit's SCHEDULE_SLOT rows in the same doctor-day transaction; a reschedule locks both doctor-days and takes the new slot rows; 100 parallel reschedules into one slot move exactly one, reschedules racing holds let exactly one win; mutation-checked (slot rows kept, new rows not taken, one day locked, guards removed)
- Left: the 100-parallel run on staging (needs MDV-P0-006)
title: No double booking under concurrency (unique index, serializable transaction, doctor-day app lock)
