confidence: 90 | Action rules per state are designed explicitly.
sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Clinician App (Schedule detail panel); docs/03-architecture/state-machines.md#appointment--visit-p1
desc:
Detail panel actions with state rules: Check in (only Booked), Reschedule (not Completed), Cancel (asks reason; not Completed/Cancelled), Mark no-show (only Booked). Drag-and-drop reschedule asks for confirmation and uses the same booking concurrency path. No-show offers "Rebook" which opens booking with the patient preselected. Reschedule/cancel notify the patient (MDV-P1-032).
ac:
- Disallowed actions are disabled with an explanation and rejected by the API if called.
- Cancel without a reason is impossible; reasons are a short list + free text.
- A reschedule keeps history (old slot, new slot, actor, time) and frees the old slot atomically.
- No-show offers rebook and is counted in the no-show metric (MDV-P1-041).

=== MDV-P1-025
status: Partly done
progress:
