sources: docs/02-design/source/Medvya Clinician App (P-01); docs/02-design/screen-specs.md#front-desk-board-p-01--medvya-clinician-app; PRD v2 finding CHECK
desc:
/front-desk board for today: Booked → Checked in → With nurse → Ready for doctor → In consult → Billing → Done with counts. Card shows name, time, doctor/visit type and nonclinical tags; CTA per column (Check in, Send to nurse, Intake done, Call in, Consult done, Payment received). "Receptionist view hides clinical notes" banner. Check-in for a returning patient: find appointment → confirm identity (name + DOB) → mark arrived, flag incomplete registration.
ac:
- A returning patient with an appointment can be checked in with ≤ 3 interactions; median check-in time is instrumented from arrival click to checked-in (exit gate 3 measurement).
- Column transitions follow the visit state machine; invalid moves are rejected server-side.
- Cards never show clinical information (reason shown only as category); verified by a security test on the board API payload.
- Billing column exists but payment actions are placeholders until P4 (feature flag).
- Board works at tablet width (horizontal scroll per responsive rules).
notes:
- Confirm the final P-01 design with the founder before build (PRD v2 finding: P-01 status "next").

=== MDV-P1-029
status: Done
progress:
- Merged [PR #83](https://github.com/ALFRED-LUCIFER/medvya/pull/83): SignalR board hub at /v1/hubs/board. Connecting needs "Check-in & queue" at the session's facility (capability policy; a refusal is audited Denied). Every call re-checks the live staff session, and Watch joins only the session's own facility after the board's access check, audited Allowed or Denied and limited per user. Groups are tenant + facility ids from the session. Messages are `{appointmentId, state, changedAt}` only (exact-field allowlist test); boards refetch the audited board endpoint
- The hub has no write methods: call-in and every status move stay on the audited HTTP endpoints with the visit state machine (409) and the in-transaction audit. Call-in records the room of the doctor's session from the template ("Called to Room 3"). After the commit, moves and bookings are pushed; a failed push never fails the move
- Client: reconnect with back-off; refetch after every (re)join, so a move is never lost or duplicated; "Live updates paused · refreshing every 30 s" (words and icon) with 30 s polling while not live; no connection while offline; stops on 401/403. Mutation-checked (13 server, 6 client); a change reaches another desk within 2 s (SQL Server, LongPolling and WebSockets); browser-verified with two signed-in desks (en, ar RTL, keyboard, axe, reconnect after killing the connection)
- Follow-ups (recorded shortcuts, not ACs): close hub connections at once when a session is revoked (MDV-P0-012); Azure SignalR Service before running more than one API instance (MDV-P0-007); Today views (P2) subscribe when they exist
