=== MDV-P1-047
title: Safe retries: idempotency keys, request timeouts and bounded retry (merges the proposed P1-047 and P1-048)
type: Story
epic: MDV-P1-E11
prd: P1-06
covers: nfr:1
priority: SHOULD
roles: Receptionist
labels: resilience, api, connectivity
estimate: 5
weeks: 11
depends: MDV-P1-021, MDV-P1-013, MDV-P1-028
confidence: 80 | Pattern is standard; the booking and check-in paths already exist; the idempotency table and client wrapper are new.
sources: docs/03-architecture/india-connectivity-power.md section 6(a); owner decision 5 Nov 2026 (047 and 048 merge, two chunks)
desc:
On flaky connections a request can reach the server while its answer never reaches the desk, and a retry must not book, check in or register twice. Server chunk: an Idempotency-Key on the booking, check-in and registration POSTs with server-side dedupe (the key is stored with the outcome, scoped to tenant and user; a repeat returns the first outcome). Client chunk: one shared API client with a 15 second timeout and bounded retry with jitter for GETs and keyed POSTs, a clear failed state that keeps the form, and the same key reused across retries of one submission. No patient data is stored in the browser.
ac:
- A booking, check-in or registration POST that repeats with the same Idempotency-Key creates exactly one record and returns the first outcome (integration test on PostgreSQL, mutation-checked: remove the dedupe and it fails).
- A retry that arrives after another user took the slot gets a conflict, the UI offers other slots, and no duplicate exists.
- The client times out after 15 seconds, shows a retry message and does not clear the form; retries are bounded, jittered and reuse the key.
- The key store holds no patient data, is scoped to tenant and user, and expired keys are removed.

=== MDV-P1-049
title: Service worker for static assets only (app shell loads with no network, no patient data)
type: Task
