sources: docs/03-architecture/india-connectivity-power.md section 6(a); deferred 5 Nov 2026
desc:
Cache the built app files (script, style, fonts) with a service worker so a reload with no network shows the app shell and an offline state instead of a browser error. Static assets only: no API response, no patient data and no identifier is cached or stored. Deferred until pilot interviews say outages are a real problem.
ac:
- With the network off, reloading a page opened earlier today loads the app shell with the offline state and shows no patient data.
- Browser storage contains no patient identifiers (automated check that fails if one appears).
- A new deploy replaces the cached files (no stale shell after a release).

